{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "hiv_ctl_nowak_bangham",
  "category": "Within-host",
  "name": "Virus dynamics with a CTL immune response",
  "description": "Within-host virus–immune-response dynamics (formulated for HIV/HTLV-1 and LCMV).\nFour compartments, and the only nonlinearity beyond standard mass action is the bilinear CTL proliferation term cz Ii Zc, which in the generator's grammar is an absolute inflow to Zc (the rate is not per-capita in a single source compartmen\nParameter values: 0 of 9 checked against the source; the rest are recalled or illustrative.",
  "reference": "Nowak MA, Bangham CRM (1996). Population dynamics of immune responses to persistent viruses. Science 272(5258):74–79",
  "referenceUrl": "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.272.5258.74",
  "time": {
    "start": "0",
    "stop": "200",
    "step": "0.2",
    "unit": "days"
  },
  "population": {
    "name": "N"
  },
